          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 \\div 3 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Such phrases are called arithmetic expressions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.373,
            0.848,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Every arithmetic expression has a value which is the number it evaluates to. For example, the value of the expression 13 + 2 is 15. This expression can be read as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } 1 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " plus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or ‘the sum of 13 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.428,
            0.848,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We use the equality sign "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\text{\" }  二  \\text{\" }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to denote the relationship between an arithmetic expression and its value. For example:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.441,
            0.468,
            0.556,
            0.488
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "13 \\pm 2 = 15."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.503,
            0.848,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Mallika spends ₹25 every day for lunch at school. Write the expression for the total amount she spends on lunch in a week from Monday to Friday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.566,
            0.648,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The expression for the total amount is 5 × 25. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 \\times 2 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " times "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or “the product of 5 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.614,
            0.848,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Different expressions can have the same value. Here are multiple ways to express the number 12, using two numbers and any of the four operations +, – , × and ÷:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.674,
            0.628,
            0.695
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "10+2,15-3,3\\times4,24\\div2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.708,
            0.847,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Choose your favourite number and write as many expressions as you can having that value."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.767,
            0.447,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Comparing Expressions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.799,
            0.848,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As we compare numbers using ‘=’, ‘<’ and ‘>’ signs, we can also compare expressions. We compare expressions based on their values and write the ‘equal "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { t o } ^ { \\flat }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , ‘greater than’ or ‘less than’ sign accordingly. For example,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.859,
            0.565,
